\title{xpam: Presence-Absence Matrix Construction from Species Range Maps}
\description{
Constructs presence-absence matrices (PAMs) from species range polygons or occurrence records. A streaming native engine rasterizes geometries onto a user-defined grid or bins them in environmental space, and returns the sites-by-species incidence as a sparse matrix plus marginals; a native Jaccard backend computes species-by-species or site-by-site similarity directly from the same incidence, at scale. A small-input dense path is kept for convenience. Includes convenience functions to retrieve example mammal range data and WorldClim environmental layers projected to two dimensions via Principal Component Analysis.
}
